    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Traditionally united by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> around 872, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> became a Christian kingdom under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-tryggvason">Olaf Tryggvason</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-ii-of-norway">Saint Olaf</a>.</li><li>Its medieval realm reached from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a> to the Baltic, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-vi-of-norway">Magnus the Lawmender</a> gave it a national law code in 1274.</li><li>After union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> from 1380 and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1814, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> became fully independent again in 1905.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-erlingsson">Magnus Erlingsson</a> was crowned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergen">Bergen</a> in 1163 or 1164, it was the first royal coronation held anywhere in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

